Frame supports still-image conversion and animated GIF output. Select a source, choose the output format in **General**, then review the relevant image or video controls.

## Still-image formats

Supported image inputs include PNG, JPEG, WebP, BMP, TIFF, AVIF, HEIC, and HEIF. Output formats are PNG, JPEG, WebP, BMP, and TIFF.

AVIF, HEIC, and HEIF are input formats in the current app; they are not output options.

## Choose image settings

The **Images** section changes with the output format:

| Format | Available controls |
| --- | --- |
| JPEG | Quality and Huffman mode |
| WebP | Lossy or lossless mode, quality, compression, and presets |
| PNG | Compression and prediction |
| TIFF | Compression selection |

Choose the format for the destination. JPEG is useful for photographs, while PNG is a common choice for graphics that need lossless storage. WebP can be useful when the receiving application supports it.

Use crop, rotation, and flipping where needed. Check output dimensions in the inspector before converting a batch of images.

